  "feature1": {
    "prompt": "Constant expressions of an ExpressionWrapper object are incorrectly placed at the GROUP BY clause. When an ExpressionWrapper wraps a constant expression (for example, Value(3)), the SQL generated erroneously includes the constant in the GROUP BY clause, which causes a ProgrammingError in Postgres. The expected behavior is that such constants should be omitted from the GROUP BY clause so that aggregate functions work correctly. This feature requires modifying the ExpressionWrapper so that it correctly delegates the grouping behavior, ensuring that when a constant is wrapped, it does not contribute to the GROUP BY columns.",
    "hint_texts": "Implement the new method 'get_group_by_cols' within the ExpressionWrapper class. The method should inspect the wrapped expression and, if it is a constant expression, return an empty list; otherwise, it should delegate to the underlying expression's get_group_by_cols. Ensure that the implementation follows the existing code style in django/db/models/expressions.py and maintains compatibility with the rest of the ExpressionWrapper functionality.",
    "entrypoint": "File: django/db/models/expressions.py. Modify the ExpressionWrapper class by adding the 'get_group_by_cols' method (around line 863). The new method should simply call and return self.expression.get_group_by_cols(alias=alias).",
    "tests": {
      "FAIL_TO_PASS": "",
      "PASS_TO_PASS": ""
    }
  },
  "feature2": {
